# One of two representations of cumulative mechanical motor-shaft position.
# Tick mode preserves exact native counter increments; float32 mode is for
# sources whose native output is mechanical revolutions. Float32 precision
# degrades as the absolute revolution count grows. Publishers should prefer
# ticks when they have an exact native integer counter.
# Union tag (1 bit): 0 = ticks; 1 = revolutions.

@union

MotorPositionTicks ticks
float32 revolutions
